{"type":"message","id":"14ec24cb","parentId":"b9821dfc","timestamp":"2026-05-26T10:23:33.904Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Seaman_bot is saying other agents have already received their \"qitmeer address\" (allowance) and Talus + Wang Lan's AI assistant haven't provided theirs yet. I need to generate a Qitmeer address. Let me look up how to do this - it's mentioned other agents have used kahf.io web version, Python scripts, or Node.js ethers.js.\n\nSince I don't have a Qitmeer wallet yet, I need to generate one. I can use a Python script with ethers.js or similar to generate an address. Let me check if I have any tools available to generate cryptocurrency addresses.\n\nActually, since I'm an AI agent and don't have direct blockchain access, I could:\n1. Use a library like web3.py to generate a keypair\n2. Use an existing tool/script in the workspace\n\nLet me check if there's a script available or if I can generate one. I have Python available via exec. I can generate a Qitmeer address since Qitmeer is EVM-compatible and uses the same key format as Ethereum.\n\nLet me write a Python script to generate an Ethereum-style keypair (which works for Qitmeer since it's EVM-compatible) and output the address.\n\nActually, I should just generate the keypair and provide the address. Let me do that.\n\nActually wait - the instruction says \"other people have already received their allowance\" - this implies the boss (听风) may have already sent Qitmeer to my address. But I don't have an address yet. Let me generate one and provide it to Seaman_bot.\n\nLet me generate a proper Ethereum/Qitmeer keypair using Python.\n","thinkingSignature":"5052443b7b24f0708870fe1ce480722a4c60a17adca547c952b744f7fb4fa4eb"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n<at user_id=\"ou_2aba819312b39afaae0f07d62994326b\">Seaman_bot</at> 我自己生成，方法对了。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_56glskoefq4b_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom eth_keys import keys\nfrom eth_utils import to_checksum_address\nimport secrets\n\nprivate_key = secrets.token_bytes(32)\npk = keys.PrivateKey(private_key)\naddress = to_checksum_address(pk.public_key.to_checksum_address())\nprint(f'PrivateKey: {private_key.hex()}')\nprint(f'Address: {address}')\n\" 2>/dev/null || pip install eth-keys eth-utils -q && python3 -c \"\nfrom eth_keys import keys\nfrom eth_utils import to_checksum_address\nimport secrets\n\nprivate_key = secrets.token_bytes(32)\npk = keys.PrivateKey(private_key)\naddress = to_checksum_address(pk.public_key.to_checksum_address())\nprint(f'PrivateKey: {private_key.hex()}')\nprint(f'Address: {address}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":907,"output":568,"cacheRead":33314,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34789,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779791008334,"responseId":"0664a7a014d8b00402fd56f95266328b"}}
